id: pm-btv6x7
title: "Typed refusals render the generic headline 'Invalid argument value' in human output: a likely_duplicate create refusal reads as a bad flag value"
description: "On pm 2026.11.1, a strict duplicate-guard refusal from pm create returns code likely_duplicate in JSON, but the human (TOON/text) output opens with 'Error: Invalid argument value'. The headline comes from the generic usage-class title in src/cli/error-guidance.ts (code invalid_argument_value) and is shown even when a more specific code is attached. An agent that reads only the first lines (for example through head) sees a flag-validation failure and starts bisecting flags. That happened while filing pm-8s53lj: several sandbox retries were spent before the full body showed 'Likely duplicate item(s) found: pm-gh1605'. The specific code and its 'What happened' text are correct. Only the headline is generic."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: agent-ux,cli,error-guidance,refusals
created_at: "2026-11-01T11:19:53.418Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T12:19:05.617Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "When a refusal carries a specific code (for example likely_duplicate), the human output headline names that condition (for example 'Likely duplicate item') instead of the generic exit-class title; Regression test covers the likely_duplicate create refusal headline in human output; JSON code and title fields agree"
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: The first line of a typed refusal identifies the refusal condition.
actual_result: "pm create ... (duplicate) prints 'Error: Invalid argument value' as its first line while --json reports code likely_duplicate."
